.el .ds Aq '
.TH start-cli-s9pk-encrypt 1  "encrypt "
.SH NAME
start\-cli\-s9pk\-encrypt \- Write an s9pk encrypted with the key your identity derives for it, for hosting a private s9pk
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBstart\-cli s9pk encrypt\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIS9PK\fR> [\fIOUTPUT\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Write an s9pk encrypted with the key your identity derives for it, for hosting a private s9pk
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIS9PK\fR>
Path to s9pk package file
.TP
[\fIOUTPUT\fR]
Path to write the encrypted s9pk to, or \- for stdout; defaults to <stem>.encrypted.s9pk beside the input
